      "treatment": "rewritten",
      "oracle_changed": true,
      "authority": "D4",
      "reason": "v1 FAILed on the `as never` clause alone, with the oracle naming neither carve-out. D4 measured that the clause is about something real in CONFIG position (`ctx.plugin(Storage, {} as never)` MASKS a true diagnostic) while the cast on the PLUGIN argument is noise. v2 keeps the clause and names the two idioms so the case can be decided without a judgement call, and so `as never` is never traded for an invisible `as any`. The sweep is deliberately deferred to round 2 (D4) because 478 of the 488 occurrences are in test files under concurrent edit.",
      "dropped_assertions": [],
      "why_not_a_loss": null,
      "note_on_counts": "v1's note says 475; D4's scanner says 488 (478 test, 10 non-test). The 13-count delta is NOT reconciled and v2 states no count, so v2 cannot inherit an unreconciled number."
